<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bellovesus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">legendary, c. 600 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bellovesus was a legendary Gallic leader, nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambigatus">Ambigatus</a> of the Bituriges, who according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> led a great migration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> around 600 BCE. Livy says his followers defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino">Ticino</a> and founded Mediolanum, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. The story reflects later Roman memory of Celtic settlement in the Po valley.</p></div>
